diff --git a/DNS_GUARD_IPQ32.md b/DNS_GUARD_IPQ32.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..57aedaf
--- /dev/null
+++ b/DNS_GUARD_IPQ32.md
@@ -0,0 +1,38 @@
+# fancyss DNS Guard for IPQ32
+
+This build is based on fancyss 3.5.30, upstream commit
+`b19e82cb6a05e08990a96905353921819d44d134`, and targets the 32-bit QCA
+IPQ53xx package used by ASUS ZenWiFi BD4 (IPQ5322, ARMv7). The official base
+package MD5 is `5519268d19fa1895456b19a4a03032d7`.
+
+## Modes
+
+- Off: fancyss keeps the user's existing DNS plan and upstream selections.
+- Standard: fancyss switches to SmartDNS, uses encrypted DNS-over-TLS upstreams,
+  redirects LAN TCP/UDP port 53 to the router, and blocks unresolved IPv4/IPv6
+  plaintext DNS forwarding.
+- Strict: includes Standard mode and also blocks plaintext TCP/UDP port 53 from
+  router-originated traffic. Local loopback DNS remains allowed.
+
+The encrypted upstreams use fixed bootstrap IP addresses, so starting DNS Guard
+does not require a plaintext DNS lookup first. The domestic group uses Alibaba
+DNS and DNSPod directly. The foreign group uses Cloudflare and Google through
+the active fancyss proxy.
+
+## Installation
+
+Upload `fancyss_ipq32_full_dnsguard.tar.gz` through the router software center's
+offline installation page. Installation does not download any components.
+
+Start with Standard mode. Use Strict mode only after Standard mode has been
+confirmed working with the active node and the router has a correct system time.
+
+## Rollback
+
+Select Off and apply the fancyss settings. Disabling or uninstalling fancyss
+also removes all DNS Guard chains because they use the normal fancyss firewall
+lifecycle and `SHADOWSOCKS*` chain namespace.
+
+This build has been statically checked and package-verified on macOS, but still
+requires acceptance testing on a physical BD4 before it should be treated as a
+production release.
diff --git a/build_dns_guard_ipq32.sh b/build_dns_guard_ipq32.sh
new file mode 100755
